One change mark instead of two — 18 Sept.

Ali: "these icons swaps are confusing - in the way of the initials and just not intuitive. 2
symbols is too much anyway" · "its not the porcess of swapping its how its displayed if swapped
short notice or if not same as rota" · "go with option one for marks".

WHAT WAS WRONG. Two 15px circles carrying the SAME swap glyph, in adjacent corners of the same
small object, told apart only by a grey-or-amber fill — and both anchored on the first letter of
the initials, so "JR" read as "R". The eye could not separate them, so it read them as
decoration and stopped looking.

WHAT IT IS NOW. One dot, in its own column before the name, where it cannot touch a letter. One
shape carrying two independent facts, which is what lets it say four things:

    FILL = WHEN        nothing · grey, moved in the last two days · amber, within a day of the
                       shift
    RING = THE SHEET   amber, when the board no longer matches the rota sheet

A hollow ring is "differs, nothing moved lately". A solid amber dot with a halo is "changed at
short notice AND the sheet has not caught up" — the state that matters most, and now the loudest
mark on the card, which it never was as two identical circles. Both sentences are joined into one
title rather than shown as two objects, because when both are true they are one story.

A blank dot is drawn on every cell so the names line up down the column. It has no title, no tap
halo and no cursor — it is spacing, not a control.

THE PROBE CAUGHT A REAL TRAP. tests/chip-probe.js asked for "td.col-B .chgdot" and got MONDAY's
blank dot, because the old selectors only ever worked while an unchanged cell had no mark at all.
The dot now carries data-d and data-k, and the probe asks for the day and the pod by name.

Tests: chip-probe 80 passed / 0 failed (rewritten for one mark, plus three new assertions that
the two-chip markup is gone rather than merely unused) · render 61/0 · attn-probe 19/0.
cover-tests and consultant-tests crash on a missing repos/allocate-pull/cover_sync.py — a path
that does not exist in this clone, unrelated to this change and failing the same way before it.
